# Force LF for everything in .github/, for the same reason images/.gitattributes
# does it: these files are consumed by Linux.
#
# A workflow every `run:` block of which is executed by bash on an ubuntu
# runner cannot survive a CRLF checkout - a trailing \r becomes part of the
# last argument on every line, and the failure ("command not found" naming a
# command that plainly exists) wastes an afternoon. The scanners are executed
# the same way.
#
# core.autocrlf=input on the maintainer's machine already normalises on
# commit, but that is a per-clone setting and this must not depend on how a
# contributor happened to configure git.
* text eol=lf
